  "note": "0.5 dev.1 (Osama, 6 November 2026). 0.5's defining feature is accuracy. Unguided anti-tank fire scatters twice as far: every tank and main-gun round (weapon type 110) and every rocket-launcher round (types 62 and 63) has its horizontal and vertical dispersion radius doubled. Guided missiles, including gun-launched ones, are unchanged. Factor 2.0 is a first test value; FREEDOM_ARROW_FIRE_STATS in the log measures the hit rate. Not deployed. 0.5 dev.2 (Osama, 6 November 2026): launcher rounds (weapon types 62 and 63) use radius 2.14/2.14 with DispersionMinimal 0.88 in place of x2: calculated 80% to hit a tank front point blank, 72% at half range, 65% at max range (crew error). Tank-gun rounds keep dev.1's x2. 0.5 dev.9 (Osama, 6 November 2026): tank-gun rounds are back to vanilla dispersion; dev.1's x2 on them is removed (70 rounds). Only launcher rounds keep a dispersion change. 0.5 dev.10 (Osama, 6 November 2026): the launcher close-range floor is removed (DispersionMinimal back to vanilla 0); launchers keep radius 2.14, so they hit 100% close in and about 65% at max range. 0.5 dev.11 (Osama, 6 November 2026): launchers radius 1.96 / 1.96, about 75% to hit a tank front at max range (was 2.14, 65%). 0.5 dev.12 (Osama, 6 November 2026): back to vanilla accuracy. Launcher radius and the ground ATGM 75% are removed; every round uses its vanilla dispersion and missile accuracy. The fire statistics in the log stay.",
